Put a .code16 or .code32 directive ahead of .arch in the x86 assembly iPXE
shares between its BIOS and x86_64 EFI builds. GNU as 2.41 and later reject
.arch i386 and .arch i586 while the assembler is still in 64-bit mode, so
without this every one of these files fails in the bin-x86_64-efi build that
the efi-*.rom NIC option ROMs come from.

